  message: "DONE, PR #1188 (merged 2026-09-24; commit dbe8541ae4).\n\nlibrary_signatures/go.yaml gains a `package_variables` section, read by load_library_package_variables with the same validation and user channel as `signatures`:\n- http.DefaultClient: http.Client\n- http.DefaultTransport: http.Transport\n- net.DefaultResolver: net.Resolver\nENUMERATED, as the row asked. Rowed only where the type carries catalogued methods. Refused with reasons in the file: os.Stdin/Stdout/Stderr (os.File has no method rows; the std streams go through io_target_kind), http.DefaultServeMux, flag.CommandLine, crypto/rand.Reader, io.Discard.\ngo.py: a call on a catalogued `pkg.Var` takes the type's package as its slot, as a typed struct field already did. The key is the package NAME, so a renamed import resolves.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE:\n- ACCEPTANCE, as filed: the go_req fixture with NewRequest deleted reads VIOLATED at net/http.Do, ddg confirmed (pinned arm C). On dev, the same deletion gave inconclusive.\n- test_go_package_variable_receiver.py, red on dev and green on the fix: DefaultClient.Do and nethttp.DefaultClient.Do classify as net/http.Client.Do (net_send); net.DefaultResolver.LookupHost classifies as net_recv; control, http.NoBody.Close stays external.\n- Go analyzer alone, pinned dev vs fix, calls edges by site. 79 sites changed, and EVERY one was a FALSE in-repo resolution of the bare name `Do`/`Get`:\n    keda     2 (HTTPDoer.Do)\n    loki    15 (Frontend.Do)\n    grafana 62 (httpClient.Do)\n  All now go to net/http. Correction to the row: on these repos the defect was false edges into project methods, not the external slot. 78 of the 79 are test code.\n- verify-claims, generic taint claims, keda and loki: 0 finding changes dev -> fix.\nInstruments: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jikik_09242026/ (FX_AB.txt, SITEDIFF.txt, vc/)."  # 8078
